      <p>In OpenShift Container Platform with OVN-Kubernetes, you can disable IP multicast on a per-project basis so pods no longer receive multicast traffic.</p>
      <h2 id="nw-disabling-multicast_ovn-kubernetes-disabling-multicast" class="group scroll-mt-20">Disabling multicast between pods<a href="#nw-disabling-multicast_ovn-kubernetes-disabling-multicast" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p class="_abstract">To disable multicast between pods in a project, you can remove the <code>k8s.ovn.org/multicast-enabled</code> annotation from the namespace by using the <code>oc annotate</code> command or a namespace manifest.</p>
      <p><strong>Prerequisites</strong></p>
      <ul>
      <li>Install the OpenShift CLI (<code>oc</code>).</li>
      <li>You must log in to the cluster with a user that has the <code>cluster-admin</code> role.</li>
      </ul>
      <p><strong>Procedure</strong></p>
      <ul>
      <li>
      Disable multicast by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc annotate {{ namespace }} <namespace> \\\n    {{ annotation }}"} lang="terminal" />
      <p>For <code>&lt;namespace&gt;</code>, specify the namespace for the project you want to disable multicast for.</p>
      <Alert variant="tip" class="my-4">
        <AlertTitle>Tip</AlertTitle>
        <AlertDescription>
          <p>You can alternatively apply the following YAML to delete the annotation:</p>
          <CodeBlock code={"apiVersion: v1\nkind: Namespace\nmetadata:\n  name: <namespace>\n  annotations:\n    k8s.ovn.org/multicast-enabled: null"} lang="yaml" />
        </AlertDescription>
      </Alert>
      </li>
      </ul>
